    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Right ankle pain after turning it on a trail run yesterday. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Turing is a 41-year-old mathematician recovering from the effects of a year of high-dose estrogen given without his consent, and in treatment for a moderate depressive episode with psychotherapy and bupropion XL 150 mg, who asked for a same-day visit. Yesterday evening, about 12 km into a trail run, he turned his right foot inward on a root and felt pain on the outside of the ankle. He walked the last kilometer home slowly. The ankle swelled overnight. The pain is 5 of 10, on the outer side, worse on walking and eased by rest and ice. He heard no pop, did not fall, and has no numbness or calf pain. He has had no earlier ankle injuries. His mood has stayed much better; he is frustrated mainly because running has been his most reliable way of managing his mood, and he is worried about losing it. He has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mechanism</td><td>Inversion injury on a trail run yesterday evening</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Outer right ankle; no foot or calf pain</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>5 of 10; walked home slowly</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Bupropion XL 150 mg and cholecalciferol; no pain medicine taken yet</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Much improved; worried about losing running; no suicidal thoughts</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

