  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right lateral ankle sprain (S93.401A)</content>. Mild to moderate lateral ligament sprain. He can bear weight and has no bony tenderness at the malleoli, the base of the fifth metatarsal, or the navicular, so the Ottawa ankle rules say no X-ray is needed. No sign of a high ankle sprain or Achilles injury. [S]<list><item>Ice for 15 minutes several times a day for two days, compression wrap, and elevation; walk as comfort allows.</item><item>Ibuprofen 400 mg up to three times a day with food for no more than 5 days; no interaction with bupropion.</item><item>Ankle range-of-motion and balance exercises from the third day; a lace-up brace for running for six weeks.</item><item>Cycling or swimming in place of running for about two weeks, then a graded return on even ground.</item><item>Return if he cannot bear weight, if the pain is worse after a week, or if bony tenderness develops.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, single episode, improving (F32.1)</content>. Responding to psychotherapy and bupropion. A pause from running is a risk to his routine, so other exercise is planned. Safety reviewed: no suicidal thoughts, intent, or plan; protective factors unchanged. [S]<list><item>Continue bupropion XL 150 mg and psychotherapy.</item><item>Swim or cycle on the days he would have run, and keep meeting his running friends.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); A study to develop clinical decision rules for the use of radiography in acute ankle injuries (1992)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Return if not improving in a week or at once for the warning signs above. Six-month review in October. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: six-month review of gynecomastia and depression in continuation treatment. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
